nebflow.llm.decision.JevAllocatorSpec:
  + the question set is one batched call with need_/fit_ pairs 0.003s
  + the whole set rides ONE request (the batch property) 0.004s
  + membership is probabilities[yes] >= 0.5 and is read from the choice answer 0.001s
  + a fit score is never used as a membership threshold 0.001s
  + a noul answer can never satisfy a need_ question 0.001s
  + a missing need_ answer shrinks the set conservatively rather than granting 0.0s
  + an empty catalog yields the empty set without spending a call 0.016s
  + a provider failure falls back and never escapes as an exception 0.006s
  + a provider timeout is classified as a timeout fallback 0.004s
  + fallback kind is decided by the typed error, not by matching its wording 0.003s
  + a thrown defect still lands on the fallback rather than the caller 0.002s
  + a successful allocation records the chosen set (the #8 'action happened' evidence) 0.003s
  + the state carries the capability catalog, each entry as name + description 0.002s
  + the catalog keeps catalog order and both section headers are present 0.003s
  + the brief cap bounds the BRIEF and cannot crowd out the catalog 0.002s
  + the question instructions are the transferred scorer's words, character for character 0.0s
  + the need_ criteria label is the transferred scorer's wording, not a paraphrase 0.0s
  + the state handed over is capped so a huge task cannot blow the budget 0.002s
