nebflow.llm.HealthHalfOpenSpec:
  + T1: a Down candidate inside the backoff window is still SKIPPED — with the wait spelled out 0.004s
  + T2: once the backoff expires the candidate is put back on the chain for a REAL try (half-open) 0.007s
  + T2b: the READ faces (panel current / waitForAnyUp) never consume a half-open slot 0.002s
  + T3: real failures re-arm a LONGER backoff each time (60s → 120s → 240s → 480s → 600s cap) 0.005s
  + T4: a successful half-open trial clears the ladder — the next Down starts again at base 0.003s
  + T5: DOWN entries whose ref left the config are dropped (phantom DOWN must not accumulate) 0.005s
  + T6: a probe failure REFRESHES the Down reason and carries the full cause chain (class names included) 0.005s
  + T7: the probe loop survives a throwing cycle instead of dying silently (the only passive recovery path) 0.606s
nebflow.llm.FallbackRetryPolicySpec:
  + TurnBudgetExceeded is classified Permanent (llm-fail retry must not fire) 0.005s
  + overload-class errors are classified Transient (retryable at fallback layer) 0.001s
  + overload retry delay is always ≥60s (rate window), regardless of backoff ramp 0.001s
  + non-overload transients keep the normal exponential ramp 0.001s
  + retry delay is capped at MaxBackoffMs for overload class when floor < MaxBackoffMs 0.0s
  + gate-wedge: StuckAbort is classified Fatal — no provider fallback, no markDown 0.001s
