nebflow.llm.decision.PluginAllocatorFallbackSpec:
  + fallback on timeout: jev leg times out → llm leg takes over, the allocation is NOT lost 0.011s
  + fallback on auth failure: jev leg 401s → llm leg takes over (超时/网络/鉴权一视同仁) 0.002s
  + leg bookkeeping: jev down + llm took over → channel Up but legs show jev Down + llm Up 0.009s
  + leg bookkeeping in toJson: the fallback story reaches the REST face (设置面「已回退 llm」数据源) 0.002s
  + fallback then llm leg fails too → channel Down with the llm reason; both legs recorded down 0.003s
  + gate off → only the llm leg is recorded (the jev leg never ran); the channel stays Up on llm success 0.001s
  + jev leg healthy → legs record jev Up only; the llm leg is never consulted 0.003s
  + legacy faces unaffected: a plain success/failure write keeps the tri-state semantics (transport write path) 0.001s
nebflow.llm.NetworkUnreachableWaitSpec:
  + 10-21 incident shape [Timeout(Permanent), Unknown(Transient)] is waitable 0.0s
  + pure connect-refused chain is waitable 0.001s
  + connection-reset chain is waitable 0.0s
  + 401/403 auth in the chain is NOT waitable — explicit rejection waits for no one 0.0s
  + pure auth chain is NOT waitable 0.0s
  + format(400) in the chain is NOT waitable 0.0s
  + model-not-found(404) in the chain is NOT waitable 0.0s
  + pure overload chain is NOT network-waitable (existing LlmTransient freeze owns it) 0.0s
  + empty attempt list is not waitable (nothing known — conservative) 0.0s
  + typed JDK network exceptions are detected through the cause chain 0.001s
  + plain SocketException stays OUT of the typed set (mid-stream reset keeps the short-freeze path) 0.0s
  + non-network errors are not typed network-unreachable 0.0s
  + classifyError maps typed network failures to NetworkUnreachable/Transient 0.0s
